```typescript
interface BlockedTaskSummary {
  ref: string;
  title: string;
  blocked_by: string[];
  unmet_deps: string[];
  unlocks: number;
}
```
Missing `slug` and `description` compared to the format file version.

---

#### Interfaces unique to a single file

**session-start-format.test.ts only:**
```typescript
interface ActiveTaskSummary {
  ref: string;
  slug: string | null;
  title: string;
  description: string | null;
  status: 'in_progress' | 'needs_work' | 'pending_review';
  started_at: string | null;
  priority: number;
  spec_ref: string | null;
  note_count: number;
  last_note_at: string | null;
  todo_count: number;
  incomplete_todos: number;
}

interface NoteSummary {
  task_ref: string;
  task_title: string;
  task_status: 'in_progress' | 'pending_review' | 'needs_work' | 'completed';
  note_ulid: string;
  created_at: string;
  author: string | null;
  content: string;
}
```

Note: `NoteSummary` is structurally identical to the inline anonymous array type in `session-start-notes.test.ts`'s `SessionContext.recent_notes`, but in format.test.ts it is a named interface with an additional `needs_work` in the `task_status` union.

**session-start-inbox-triage.test.ts only:**
```typescript
interface InboxSummary {
  ref: string;
  text: string;
  created_at: string;
  tags: string[];
  added_by: string | null;
  triaged: boolean;
  triage_action: string | null;
}
```

**session-start-computed-json.test.ts only:**
```typescript
interface SessionContextComputed {
  inbox_untriaged_count: number;
  inbox_deferred_count: number;
  inbox_total: number;
  task_unlocks: Record<string, number>;
  recent_activity: ActivityItem[];
}
```

---

### Summary Table

| Name | Files | Identical? |
|---|---|---|
| `addInboxItem()` | computed-json, inbox-triage | Yes — exact duplicate |
| `triageItem()` | computed-json, inbox-triage | Yes — body identical, JSDoc differs slightly |
| `ActivityItem` | activity-timeline, format, computed-json | No — computed-json uses inline anonymous types; activity-timeline/format match structurally but reference different local `CompletedTaskSummary` |
| `CommitSummary` | activity-timeline, format | Yes — exact duplicate |
| `CompletedTaskSummary` | activity-timeline, format | No — format adds `slug: string | null` |
| `InboxStats` | format, inbox-triage | Yes — exact duplicate |
| `SessionContext` | all 6 files | No — each file defines a narrow projection of the real shape |
| `ReadyTaskSummary` | format, unlocks | No — format adds `slug` and `description` |
| `BlockedTaskSummary` | format, unlocks | No — format adds `slug` and `description` |
| `NoteSummary` (named) vs anonymous | format vs notes | Near-duplicate — format adds `needs_work` to `task_status` union |

### Key Consolidation Opportunities

The **two most clear-cut duplicates** ready to extract to a shared location are:

1. `addInboxItem()` and `triageItem()` — byte-for-byte identical function bodies in `session-start-computed-json.test.ts` and `session-start-inbox-triage.test.ts`. These could move to `/workspace/tests/helpers/cli.ts` or a new `tests/helpers/session-helpers.ts`.

2. `CommitSummary` and `InboxStats` — exact structural duplicates across two files each.

The `SessionContext` interface is deliberately narrow in each file (each test file only needs the fields it exercises), so consolidation there is less straightforward — a full canonical `SessionContext` type would need to be a superset, and each file would then only use a subset of it.

