Fix removeAllListeners() in readStdinIfAvailable to use named handlers
────────────────────────────────────────
ULID:      01KJ9ZJPKKHWSJZT2E289J9B1Z
Type:      bug
Status:    pending
Priority:  2
Automation: eligible

─── Description ───
  In src/cli/commands/session.ts, the readStdinIfAvailable() function (~line 1669-1696) calls process.stdin.removeAllListeners() in its timeout handler. This removes ALL stdin listeners, not just the ones this function added, which could break other code with stdin listeners.

  Fix: Replace with named handler functions and use process.stdin.removeListener(event, handler) to only clean up the specific handlers this function registered.

  Current pattern:
    process.stdin.removeAllListeners()

  Should be:
    const onData = (chunk) => { ... };
    const onEnd = () => { ... };
    process.stdin.on('data', onData);
    process.stdin.on('end', onEnd);
    // In cleanup:
    process.stdin.removeListener('data', onData);
